  18: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  19:     """Erase the first border pixel hit by extending the red marker away from its pink trail.
  20: 
  21:     Input structure
  22:     - The dominant background surrounds a unique red marker and a four-pixel
  23:       pink trail.
  24:     - The pink pixels form one straight 8-connected ray starting next to the
  25:       red marker.
  26:     - In the opposite direction from that trail, the red marker faces a
  27:       non-background border or obstacle pixel beyond background cells.
  28: 
  29:     Rule
  30:     - Keep the whole grid fixed except for the first non-background pixel on
  31:       the ray from the red marker away from the pink trail.
  32:     - Recolor that one hit pixel to the background color.
  33: 
  34:     Key insight
  35:     - The pink trail marks where the red marker came from, so the edit is found
  36:       by ray-casting from the red marker in the opposite direction.
  37:     """
  38:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  39:     assert g.ndim == 2
  40:     H, W = g.shape
  41:     bg = get_bg(g)
